findings={
 'tim-rpn-call-state':[
 'FALSIFIED exact parameter identity: rpn_dual_parameters is Java-valid and has exact source plain/dollar / cedar/larch; candidate emits /dollar / /larch. Direct-read control rpn_bare_read removes the GetVariableValue confound: Java plain/dollar, Rust b/dollar. Both existed before too; neither is a newly lost pass.',
 'Java TFunctionArgument.getName -> TFunctionImpl.getNewMemory -> TMemoryLocal preserves b and $b as distinct map keys. Rust parse_func_params now preserves spelling for matching but call_function_values strips the dollar at the memory boundary and overwrites the bare slot. prepare_expression cannot resolve a bare local, and GetVariableValue only checks token_defines for bare names. Exact binding is not confined to signature matching.',
 'The expression-wide Vec/HashMap lifetime, distinct-key operand count, clearing after a call, and independent function-body expression sessions follow ReversePolishInterpretor. rpn_spelling_body, rpn_nested_consumption and rpn_neighbor_calls match exact source and actual CLI SVG. The duplicate-key control now rejects through fatal underflow, whereas Java throws NoSuchElementException and produces empty output. This is rejection evidence, not diagnostic/negative-output parity.',
 'No new label-keyed branch or unexplained constant found. This is a real incomplete generative memory model, not a fixture workaround.'
 ],
 'tim-call-operand-resolution':[
 'FALSIFIED signature coverage across declared overloads: operand_overload_return defines a one-argument return function then a two-argument procedure. Java resolves the one-argument function and renders value 7; Rust reports Unknown built-in function $pick. Reversing declaration kinds/order in operand_overload_procedure lets Java emit alder/beech while Rust again errors. Both are valid references and pre-existing candidate-before errors.',
 'Java FunctionsSet.functions keys by TFunctionSignature and getFunctionSmart first checks exact positional signature then canCover. Rust PreprocessContext.functions is HashMap<String, FunctionDef>, and try_function_def inserts by name alone, overwriting the earlier arity. execute_expression_into and call_function_values therefore check coverage/kind against an incomplete set. Reordering the kind check is insufficient to establish the claimed signature-resolution invariant.',
 'Bounded plain named-RHS behavior survives: duplicate ignored named operands execute their RHS in order without increasing positional arity; operand_duplicate_effects and operand_plain_exact_shortcut match source/SVG. The named-RHS conversion error precedes failed strlen coverage. Missing procedure coverage reports Unknown built-in function; covered procedure reports Illegal call here. These first error messages match, without claiming exact negative SVG or partial-source parity.',
 'No new builtins added or audited for breadth. Registry, arity table, comparator and skips are unchanged; no fixture-shaped selection found in the production diff.'
 ],
 'tim-legacy-raw-caller-prefix':[
 'Fresh bounded observations survive. legacy_repeated_raw varies variable/function prefixes, indentation, arguments and repeated invocations; exact Java source and source-only CLI SVG match. legacy_procedure_control keeps the evaluated prefix and suffix for a procedure, while the multiline legacy suffix is dropped. A failing prefix conversion aborts before macro expansion.',
 'Java TContext.applyFunctionsAndVariables sets pendingAdd to str.getString().substring(0,i) for LEGACY_DEFINELONG and result.toString() for PROCEDURE; Rust uses line[..offset] only for multiline legacy. The change has direct causal provenance and no tuned constants or fixture-shaped branch.',
 'This does not establish complete legacy macro-body semantics, zero/one/many emitted-event behavior, or whole TIM. Mandatory standing/main/guard gates remain red; green bounded observations are not acceptance.'
 ],
 'tim-local-sub-collection':[
 'FALSIFIED collection before function buffering. sub_uncalled_function has nested local markers inside an uncalled procedure. Java rejects Cannot nest sub during initial collection; Rust exits zero and retains class Survivor. The valid companion sub_defined_in_uncalled registers a subblock in that procedure and includes it outside: Java emits class Kept; Rust errors cannot include stored.',
 'Java TContext.buildCodeIterator wraps CodeIteratorSub before CodeIteratorReturnFunction and CodeIteratorProcedure, so their body collection traverses sub processing. Rust execute_one_line checks an already active collecting_sub early, but recognition of a new !startsub occurs after try_function_def. While collecting a function the latter consumes every marker, so the new nested check never activates until a call (or never at all).',
 'Top-level collection-before-effects is supported: sub_collect_error_precedence contains an earlier invalid IntVal and an inactive nested marker, and both implementations report Cannot nest sub first. Comment removal and replay count pass sub_comment_replay. These controls do not close the iterator-order gap.',
 'Java CLI diagnostic line zero versus located Rust line remains residual for nesting; error-message agreement does not establish negative-output equality. Existing external raw-sub selection and raw !endsub0 downstream class acceptance are untouched.'
 ],
 'tim-intval-conversion':[
 'The explicitly bounded ASCII planned change survives fresh sign/range/type controls: -000, +2147483647, JSON-displayed -2147483648, invalid +-3 and negative overflow. Exact valid source/SVG matches; invalid conversion remains the first diagnostic before a later bad strlen call.',
 'The account invariant read without its ASCII qualification is false. Two fresh Java-valid cases use +fullwidth digits and -Arabic-Indic digits, and mixed ASCII/Devanagari through a JSON string. Java Integer.parseInt converts them to 123/-42 and 123; Rust str::parse::<i32> rejects both. Before rendered invented zero values and after now errors, so these are new valid CLI errors in the fresh matrix, not lost valid SVG passes.',
 'This Unicode limitation was explicitly excluded in the precommitted planned_change, not invented after this review. It does not disprove strict ASCII conversion, but prevents claiming complete displayed-TValue/Integer.parseInt equivalence. Preserve the counterexamples and scope visibly; do not add them to skips or call Java-invalid.',
 'No fixture-specific conversion constants or fallback values were introduced. No whole conversion acceptance follows while the standing/guard gates remain red.'
 ],
 'tim-hsl-typed-alpha':[
 'Fresh bounded observations survive: hsl_rounding_extremes covers maximum/minimum signed hue before float conversion, wrapped hue and 1/50/99 percent alpha; hsl_typed_channels covers string/JSON integer-field semantics, negative lightness and out-of-range saturation/alpha; hsl_named_alpha distinguishes ignored plain named operands and JSON alpha. All three valid cases match exact source and actual CLI SVG. hsl_bad_arity preserves conversion-error precedence.',
 'Audited Java HslColor -> TValue.toInt -> HSLColor.toRGB/HueToRGB -> XColor.fromFloat -> HColorSimple.asString. Rust f32 operation order, double alpha division before f32 cast, signed remainder, clamping, channel rounding and transparent/uppercase RGB/lowercase ARGB serialization match the cited model. Constants 360,100,1/3,2/3,6,2,3,0.5,255 have adjacent source provenance; no tuned threshold or fixture branch found.',
 'This review is bounded to these typed operands/equations/serialization, not the unrelated f64 lighten/darken helper, palette/style/rendering, all builtins or all input grammar. Mandatory gates remain red, so observations cannot be an accepted mechanism record.'
 ]}
